{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nEach application domain defines what identifies a node across runs. Changes to a node's contents or outgoing edges preserve its identity.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations from `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types`: (1) each application domain defines what identifies a node across runs; (2) changes to a node's contents or outgoing edges preserve that identity. `requirements.sdk.domain` is cited context only.\n\n**(1) Identity defined and stable across runs.**\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` builds every `HabeasNode` kind. It asserts the exact `node_path` segments for each kind.\n  - It asserts the paths are pairwise distinct.\n  - It asserts a freshly constructed `HabeasDomain` with a new `OutlineCache` gives an equal path for the same node data.\n  - It asserts that changing the scheme, the location, or the selector yields a different identity.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[enum_node_ids_distinguish_requirements_and_source_items_in_one_domain]` covers the enum-identified domain. It asserts distinct paths for requirement and source nodes, and equal paths across a fresh `ReviewDomain`. It also asserts that evidence stored under one node's identity is not loaded for the other node.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` asserts that opaque node data gives stable, distinct node paths. It also asserts that edges are resolved by identity.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` stores a record and loads it back by the same node and criterion.\n\n**(2) Identity preserved under changes to contents or edges.**\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` changes a source file's contents. It reconstructs the domain and recovers the node's data from the old interned node. It re-interns that data in the new domain and reads the new content. The fingerprint differs while the node is still reachable by the same identity.\n  - The same test adds a reference to the file, so the requirement's outgoing `Implements` edges go from empty to one. The requirement node is still found by the same data, and the saved record's `is_current` check resolves the same nodes and reports them stale.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_shares_discovery_snapshots_with_tracked_reads]` edits the file after discovery and shows the node keeps the same path and data while the content is reread.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` stores a record and loads it back by node identity. `fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` records a dependency on the node that was read.\n\nA domain that derived identity from content or from edge sets would fail the Habeas tests. Those tests re-intern the same data after the content or edges change, and they require the same path and a retrievable node. I found no unmarked relevant tests and no acknowledgments. I judge the tests adequate.",
  "references": "78521c46b3d7e947f2b1c262b4ddec789e08bce27062b8e4b6647057a600a11c",
